# Root build context (web-app's Dockerfile uses `context: .` so it can build the
# sibling behavior-sdk/ package). Without this, `COPY web-app/ ./` and
# `COPY behavior-sdk/ ./` run *after* their own `RUN npm install` and would overwrite
# the freshly-installed, in-container node_modules with whatever node_modules exists
# on the host -- on this Windows host that bakes in a literal `file:../behavior-sdk`
# symlink pointing at a Windows path (`C:/vs code/...`), which doesn't resolve inside
# the Linux container and breaks Vite's import resolution for `@cogniguard/behavior-sdk`.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.git
